  "description": "Frozen five-task state-only rollout evaluation. The scientific scope of the experiment (final evaluation plan, sec. 3): one row per (method, task, seed). Lift is the first debugging task because its geometry is the simplest, but the reported results cover all five benchmark tasks (Lift, Can, Square, ToolHang, Transport). Each task is evaluated as a separate single-task policy (not a multi-task policy). The same 10-method matrix is replicated for each task: the canonical PhaseForge proposed method (six experts, centroid router, 50% partial warm-start — R50 promoted to the phaseforge identity), the dense floors (BC-MLP, parameter-matched BC-Large), the temporal BC-RNN comparator, and the MoE architecture/warm-start/router/representation controls. Oracle ground-truth routing is NOT a training cell: it is applied post-hoc at evaluation time on the fixed trained expert set via `eval_mode='oracle'` in `phaseforge/models/phase_moe.py` (see research_definition.md, sec. 3 H5).",
